drm: sun50i-h713-afbd: republish the VidDec record when the geometry changes

The scaler never follows the source. With a 1280x720 signal the capture block
is rebuilt -- INCAP 0x06940874 reads 0x050002D0 -- while the scale ratio at
0x05180008 stays 0x43010000, exactly unity, and bit 27 of 0x05180014, the
firmware's "no scaling" flag, stays set. Every register in the chain behind
AFBD keeps the panel geometry. Sweeping the source, re-sending Wce_SetWindow,
running stock's full source-switch sequence and re-probing with the source
already present all changed nothing.

The reason is in this driver. Read out of the live firmware through its own
debug shell, over the monitor ring in DRAM: the VideoDec signal detector's
working copy at +0xb0 and its latch at +0x140 are byte-identical to the record
this function publishes -- 0x61770000, 0x780, 0x438 -- and they hold the
geometry that was current when the plane was first enabled. They are identical
to each other, so the firmware concludes nothing changed and never runs
UpdateWce, so WCETop::SetWindow never runs, so nothing reprograms the window
nodes. Stock's own log shows the other side of it: UpdateWce appears exactly
twice in six minutes of runtime, both at timestamp 0, and each time it walks
Cap, NR, DETN, Proc and Panel and computes a ratio with CalcScaleRatio.

The comment this patch replaces had it half right and half wrong, and the
wrong half sent this project chasing RPCs for a day. The HDMI capture really
does not read the record. The window layer does, and the window layer is what
owns the scaler.

So publish it again when the geometry changes, in ring mode only. The cost is
known and already handled: publication switches the capture off, which is why
the descriptor notifier exists and why the capture owner answers it with a
source switch away and back. A first publication already depends on that path;
this uses it a second time. Outside ring mode nothing changes -- the refusal
and its warning stand, because there the record is the plane's own frame format
and a silent change would be a lie.

diff -ruN a/drivers/gpu/drm/tiny/sun50i-h713-afbd.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/tiny/sun50i-h713-afbd.c
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/tiny/sun50i-h713-afbd.c	2026-09-07 21:11:40.896565998 +0200
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/tiny/sun50i-h713-afbd.c	2026-09-07 21:11:40.902451553 +0200
@@ -387,17 +387,28 @@
  * pointer went from nothing to the record. They are per-boot state, which is
  * also why the disable path leaves them standing.
  *
- * In HDMI passthrough (@ring) the record is published once per boot with the
- * geometry of the first enable and then left alone, whatever geometry later
- * enables bring. That is not a refusal and does not warn: the record describes
- * the *VideoDec* source and is read by the firmware's VideoDec detector alone
- * (GetFrameInfo/ConvertFrameInfo2SignalInfo). The HDMI capture and the WCE
- * behind it never look at it -- the firmware's own chain for an HDMI signal
- * change, from "AV mute" to NotifySignalChange, has no descriptor in it at all
- * (stock elog, doku/91 Punkt 2). The plane takes its geometry from the
- * framebuffer, the firmware takes its geometry from the signal, and the record
- * stands as first published for as long as the boot lasts -- the one thing the
- * firmware is known to survive.
+ * In HDMI passthrough (@ring) the record used to be published once per boot and
+ * then left alone whatever geometry later enables brought, on the reasoning
+ * that the HDMI capture and the WCE behind it never look at it. Half of that
+ * is right and the half that is wrong cost this project a long hunt.
+ *
+ * Right: the HDMI *capture* does not read it. INCAP is reconfigured on an HDMI
+ * signal change without any descriptor involved, measured -- with a 1280x720
+ * source 0x06940874 reads 0x050002D0 while the record still says 1920x1080.
+ *
+ * Wrong: the *window layer* reads it, and the window layer is what programs
+ * the scaler. Read out of the live firmware on 07.09.2026 through its own debug
+ * shell: the VideoDec detector's working copy at +0xb0 and its latch at +0x140
+ * are byte-identical to this record, both holding the geometry of the boot, and
+ * because they are identical the firmware concludes nothing changed and never
+ * runs UpdateWce. The scaler ratio at 0x05180008 then stays at unity through
+ * every source change -- which is exactly the symptom, and it is ours.
+ *
+ * So on a geometry change in ring mode the record is republished, deliberately.
+ * The known cost is that publication switches the capture off; the descriptor
+ * notifier below exists for precisely that and the capture owner answers it
+ * with a source switch. That is the same mechanism a first publication already
+ * relies on, now used a second time.
  *
  * Returns true if the firmware has something new to look at here, i.e. if the
  * record or the pointer changed. See h713_afbd_wait_wce().
@@ -414,7 +425,7 @@
 	new_ptr = readl(h->regs + AFBD_VIDEO_INFO0) != ptr;
 	h713_afbd_build_video_info(rec, w, hgt, stride);
 	differs = memcmp(h->video_info, rec, sizeof(rec)) != 0;
-	write_record = differs && !h->video_info_published;
+	write_record = differs && (!h->video_info_published || ring);
 	if (differs && h->video_info_published && !ring)
 		drm_warn(&h->drm,
 			 "refusing to rewrite the VidDec descriptor for %ux%u; the capture does not survive a second signal event\n",
